codex
I found a concrete comparability problem in the general-knowledge eval: the Qwen base model uses its native image budget, while the fine-tuned model inherits the smaller budget saved during training. That can look like forgetting even when the difference comes from image resolution.

The current Qwen LoRA regex does match the language model’s linear-attention, full-attention, and MLP projections. I found no vision-tower matches.

